## 🟡 Medium — Missing negative / edge-case tests

These scenarios have **zero coverage** and are common production bug sources:

| Missing test | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| `UpdatePrice` with nonexistent SKU | Should throw `KeyNotFoundException` — never tested |
| `GetProduct` with nonexistent SKU | Should return `null` — never tested |
| `Search` with no matches | Should return empty list |
| `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | Will throw on bad decimal / missing columns — no guard |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount` with fraction ≥ 1 | Sets prices to zero or negative — no validation |
| `ImportFromCsv` multi-line | Only tested with 1 line |

Example for the most critical missing case:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[ExpectedException(typeof(KeyNotFoundException))]
public void UpdatePrice_NonexistentSku_Throws()
{
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("NOPE", 5.00m);
}
```

